          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 495992,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "That's a good starting point. I'd also add the 'Galley' or parallel-wall layout. It's very common in apartments. So, 'I-shape', 'L-shape', and 'Galley'. That gives us three solid options to cover most scenarios.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 82913,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Three sounds right. Not too many, not too few. What about the measurement checklist for T1? What needs to be on it?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 45878,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Just wall to wall, floor to ceiling, and where the sink pipes are. Simple.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 399998,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "We should be more detailed to avoid on-site issues. What about power outlet locations for appliances? Window and door frame positions? Radiator placement? A cabinet could easily block one of those if we don't map it out first. The risk of rework is high if we miss these.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 495992,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Exactly. My experience from deliveries is that access is everything. We need to note hallway widths and tight corners too, not just the kitchen itself. I can draft a structure for the checklist in A1. It should have sections for: 1. Overall Dimensions (L/W/H), 2. Obstructions (windows, doors, pipes), 3. Utilities (plumbing, electrical, gas), and 4. Access Path.",
            "mentions": [],
