                "emoji": "saw",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M34",
            "speaker_id": 45878,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "I'll take the wall cabinets! I can get them all cut before lunch.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M35",
            "speaker_id": 82913,
            "reply_to": "M33",
            "text": "I can handle the tall cabinets. Let's make sure we're all on the same page for the build sequence. I suggest: 1. Cut all panels. 2. Edge banding. 3. Box assembly. 4. Doors/drawers. This way we can work in parallel efficiently.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D5"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M36",
            "speaker_id": 495992,
            "reply_to": "M35",
            "text": "That sequence makes sense. I'll help with assembly once parts are cut. More importantly, let's talk about quality control (T8). I've started a draft checklist in A3. Before any unit is considered 'done', I propose we make three checks mandatory: 1. All dimensions match A2, 2. Box is perfectly square, and 3. All hardware is aligned and functioning. We can't afford to fix these on-site.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T8",
              "A3",
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D6"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "clipboard",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 399998,
            "reply_to": "M36",
            "text": "Good list. We should add a check for surface blemishes *before* the finishing stage. It's much easier to fix a scratch in raw board than a finished panel. Also, let's not forget the safety guidelines in A8 while we work.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A8"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
