      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Align on packaging, loading, and on-site handling for the prototype install.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M45",
            "speaker_id": 82913,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, the prototype modules are through finishing and look great. They'll be ready for transport tomorrow. We need to finalize the plan for T5 and T6. What's our strategy for packaging and loading?",
            "mentions": [
              45878,
              399998,
              495992,
              506532
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T5",
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 495992,
            "reply_to": "M45",
            "text": "I've put together a draft procedure in A5. Based on my past work as a move coordinator, I recommend heavy-duty cardboard corner protectors on all edges, a full wrap in 1/2-inch bubble wrap, and then shrink-wrapping the whole module. This prevents scratches and impact damage.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "eyes",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 45878,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "That sounds like a lot of work. Can't we just use moving blankets? It's way faster.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 506532,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "Blankets can slip, and they don't protect corners from a hard knock. For a standardized product line, having a repeatable, professional packaging method is key. The method in A5 is solid. I support it.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 495992,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "Thanks. For the loading order (T6), I propose we load in reverse order of installation to make things smooth on-site. That means tall cabinets go in the van first, then base units, and wall units last, so they are the first ones out.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T6"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 399998,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "The loading order is logical. One addition for A5: each wrapped module needs a large, clear label stating its type (e.g., 'Base 600 Drawer'), and its intended location. This avoids confusion and unnecessary shuffling in a cramped apartment.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 3
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 495992,
            "reply_to": "M50",
            "text": "Excellent point. I'll add a labeling standard to the guideline in A5 right now. It's a small detail that makes a huge difference.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 82913,
            "reply_to": "M51",
            "text": "Okay, this all sounds great. So, are we ready to approve this combined plan? The packaging method, the labeling standard, and the reverse loading order to be our standard for this line?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 506532,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "Yes, I approve. Let's make it official.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "white_check_mark",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 45878,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "Ok.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
